## Essential Map Utility Methods

Beyond `insert` and `get`, Map provides methods for checking, removing, and counting entries.

### contains — Check for Key

```xiom
let m = Map[Str, Int]();
m.insert("Alice", 95);

let has_alice = m.contains(&"Alice");  // true
let has_dave = m.contains(&"Dave");    // false
```

Use `.contains()` when you only care about existence, not the value.

### remove — Delete Entry

```xiom
var m = Map[Str, Int]();
m.insert("temp", 42);
m.insert("keep", 100);

m.remove(&"temp");  // removes the entry for "temp"
m.contains(&"temp");  // false
m.contains(&"keep");  // true
```

### len — Count Entries

```xiom
let m = Map[Int, Str]();
m.insert(1, "one");
m.insert(2, "two");
m.insert(3, "three");

let count = m.len();  // 3
```

### Practical Patterns

```xiom
// Cache pattern: compute if missing
fn get_or_compute(m: &mut Map[Str, Int], key: Str) -> Int {
  if !m.contains(&key) {
    let computed = key.len();  // expensive computation
    m.insert(key, computed);
  }
  return m.get(&key).unwrap_or(0);
}

// Cleanup pattern: remove all entries below threshold
fn remove_below(m: &mut Map[Str, Int], threshold: Int) -> Unit {
  for key in m.keys() {
    if m.get(&key).unwrap_or(0) < threshold {
      m.remove(&key);
    }
  }
}
```

### Method Summary

| Method | Returns | Description |
|--------|---------|-------------|
| `.insert(key, val)` | Unit | Insert or update |
| `.get(&key)` | Option[V] | Lookup by key |
| `.contains(&key)` | Bool | Key existence check |
| `.remove(&key)` | Unit | Delete entry |
| `.len()` | Int | Number of entries |
| `.keys()` | Collection | All keys |
| `.values()` | Collection | All values |

